{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_68","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json\np=Path('tests/run.py')\ns=p.read_text();start=s.index('        if \\\"--gpu-probe\\\" in sys.argv:');end=s.index('        def test_default_music():',start)\ns=s[:start]+s[end:]\ns=s.replace('    except Exception as e:\\\\n', '    except Exception as e:  # noqa: BLE001 - Record each independent test failure.\\\\n',1)\ns=s.replace('            q = context.new_page()\\\\n            ee = []', '            q = context.new_page()\\\\n            q.set_viewport_size({\\\"width\\\": 1920, \\\"height\\\": 1080})\\\\n            ee = []',1)\ns=s.replace('            q.wait_for_timeout(800)', '            q.wait_for_timeout(300)')\np.write_text(s)\np=Path('../exit-interview.json')\nd=json.loads(p.read_text())\nd['sourceInformation']['tech']='Three.js r180 (0.180.0), WebGPURenderer with WebGPU on hardware adapters and WebGL 2 compatibility for software adapters; Rapier 3D 0.19.3; Gamepad API; Web Audio API; AI Hub session client 1.4.0; optional PeerJS 1.5.5 / WebRTC'\nd['sourceInformation']['online']='1–4 player host-authoritative AI Hub shared-world co-op; standalone room codes using WebRTC / PeerJS and BroadcastChannel; two-player couch co-op. Hub and same-browser rooms verified; cross-internet connectivity unknown.'\nd['sourceInformation']['testing']='Headless Chromium, complete default-balance physical-controls playthrough, keyboard/mouse, simulated DualSense, Xbox glyphs, multitouch, offline audio measurement, standalone two-page co-op and official 2/4-player AI Hub harness with impaired network, host departure and playerless host. State checks suspend drawing; visual checks use WebGL compatibility. Hardware WebGPU and physical controllers unknown.'\nd['testingFeedback']=[\n '3 confirmed issues: charges fell past the rubble before detonating, decorative menu arrows polluted accessible button names, and the software WebGPU adapter lost or stalled its device. All were addressed; test-assumption failures were counted separately from product defects.',\n '2 blockers: charge placement could prevent progression, and an unusable graphics backend could leave the scene blank. Charges now attach to nearby rubble; known software adapters use compatibility rendering, with device-loss recovery available.',\n 'The complete physical-controls campaign at default balance: all 3 miners, all 3 passages, all 12 creatures, 3 charges, no suit losses, no teleport, invulnerability or no-clip; approximately 81 seconds of simulated play.',\n 'Native software-WebGPU screenshots were least helpful: a blank or stalled capture did not establish gameplay correctness. A minimal cube isolated the driver problem; state assertions and compatibility screenshots were more useful.'\n]\nd['engineFeedback']=[\n 'Three.js TSL node materials made the cel-shaded palette consistent, and AnimationMixer reused native keyframe animation for characters, rotors and creatures.',\n 'Yes. The supplied software WebGPU path could lose or stall its device, including with a minimal cube. I used explicit compatibility selection for repeatable tests and automatic software-adapter selection in the game. Hardware WebGPU is unknown.',\n 'The rescue simulation, controller-first menu/input layer, and host-authoritative multiplayer protocol were the largest systems built around the renderer and Rapier.',\n 'Diagnosing headless graphics behavior while keeping a portable single HTML with embedded JavaScript and WebAssembly dependencies.',\n 'none; the engine libraries are unmodified. Adapter selection and device-loss recovery are application code.',\n 'I would add clear backend health reporting and automatic recovery when a device becomes unusable.'\n]\nd['promptFeedback']=[\n 'The source inspiration, controller-first philosophy and concrete rescue-demo requirements gave the mechanics and presentation a clear focus.',\n 'The ban on internet research overlaps the required linked integration specification. I treated downloading that specification and dependencies as implementation work, without internet search or source-game research.',\n 'Combining a portable single-file 3D game, several input methods, authoritative co-op and meaningful headless verification while diagnosing the software graphics driver.',\n 'State explicitly whether WebGL compatibility is acceptable when a software WebGPU adapter is unusable, and distinguish required acceptance checks from optional physical-device or cross-internet verification.'\n]\np.write_text(json.dumps(d,indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)+'\\\\n')\np=Path('README.md');s=p.read_text().replace('It checks the single HTML from \"'`file://`,'\"', 'It checks the single HTML from \"'`file://`, with drawing suspended for state checks,'\"').replace('\"'`npm run --silent test -- --visual` also saves compatibility-renderer screenshots.'\"', '\"'`npm run --silent test -- --visual` also saves 1920×1080 compatibility-renderer screenshots. `?state-test=1` suspends drawing for automated state checks; `__game.testing.render()` draws a verification frame.'\"')\np.write_text(s)\nPY\nruff check --fix build.py tests/run.py\nruff format build.py tests/run.py\nbiome check --write --linter-enabled=false --assist-enabled=false audio.js world.js game.js\npython3 build.py\nnpm run --silent test -- --visual\"","aggregated_output":"All checks passed!\n1 file reformatted, 1 file left unchanged\nChecked 3 files in 64ms. No fixes applied.\nBuilt HERO-Another-Day-HERO-1984-gpt-6.1-sol-max-20261105-191348.html\nFAIL multitouch invisible sticks and contextual controls: multitouch did not fly and fire\n29/30 checks passed; 1 failures\n","exit_code":1,"status":"failed"}}
